  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The wire is stretched to&nbsp;double its length. Therefore, if the length of the wore was&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>, change in the length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></math>.</p><p>Applying Hooke&#39;s law,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>stress</mtext><mtext>strain</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mi>A</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
